# Build context guard for docker-compose.
#
# Both `pdf` and `test` use `context: .`, so without this file every build ships
# the entire repo to the daemon — including scout/.venv (149 MB) and the DuckDB.
# Docker reads the .dockerignore beside the context root ONLY: a build run from
# here does NOT see scout/.dockerignore. If a build log shows
# `transferring context: 2B` for the ignore file, none was found.

.git/
.github/
.githooks/

# scout/ is not part of the PDF image's build context at all. Its own test image
# is built with `context: ./scout` (compose service `scout-test`), which is what
# makes scout/.dockerignore apply.
scout/

# Career artifacts the PDF renderer never reads — it only walks resumes/*.md.
A.Team/
companies/
tracking/
prep-guide/
behavioral/
profile/

**/.DS_Store
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
tmp/
scratch/
*.log
